[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613806698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100554#issuecomment-2613806698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100554","id":2613806698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6by4Zq","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T06:24:50Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T06:34:25Z","body":"> behaves like `source_signal.connect(target_function.bind(args).unbind(n))`\r\n\r\nThis is correct, see the [comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98713#issuecomment-2451567279) for reference. Any sequence of `bind()` and `unbind()` calls can be reduced to the form `.bind(...).unbind(...)`. (But I didn't look at the code, just noted that the idea is correct. I would like to review this later if I find free time.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613806698/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924296883","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100554#issuecomment-2924296883","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100554","id":2924296883,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uTTqz","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T05:01:20Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T06:16:16Z","body":"> ... and behaves like `source_signal.connect(target_function.bind(args).unbind(n))`.\r\n> \r\n\r\n~~While correct, it doesn't seem to make sense. Because whether it is `unbind(...).bind(...)` or `bind(...).unbind(...)`, the last bound arguments will be unbound first, not the original arguments. It's LIFO.~~\r\n\r\nThere is at most one `bind() `call here. So it is feasible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924296883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]